  "authority": "International Journal of Middle East Studies (Cambridge University Press), IJMES Translation and Transliteration Guide and chart",
  "description": "Anglo-American Middle East studies standard: ALA-LC consonants with ʿ (U+02BF) for ʿayn and ʾ (U+02BE) for hamza, ة = a (at in construct), ى = ā, article al- without assimilation, -iyya/-ī.",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-file-manager/file/57d83390f6ea5a022234b400/TransChart.pdf",
    "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/international-journal-of-middle-east-studies/information/author-resources/ijmes-translation-and-transliteration-guide"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "This is the full IJMES chart transliteration (technical terms). For personal names IJMES drops dots and macrons but keeps ʿ and ʾ (Jamal ʿAbd al-Nasir); strip combining marks and macrons from this output to get that form. IJMES also allows accepted English spellings of prominent people.",
    "Initial hamza is dropped; ة after alif is t (zakāt, ṣalāt); construct-state -at is not generated; final -iyy = ī, -uww = ū; diphthongs aw/ay (the chart also allows au/ai).",
    "The -l- form of the article after a prefixed particle (wa-l-, bi-l-) is not generated."
  ],
  "alphabet": "ءآأؤإئابةتثجحخدذرزسشصضطظعغفقكلمنهوىيٱپچژگڤ",
